From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ManuelArto <manuelartociao@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:02:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] fix(daisugi): check the Keccak EIP-8288 commitment of
 every Daisugi block locally

Lighthouse recomputed the block dependency hash with BLAKE2s and compared the block hash only on
optimistic finalized sync, where a mismatch was a warning. Hash with Keccak-256 as Nethermind does,
split the lists by scheme equality, and reject a Daisugi block whose recomputed hash differs on every
import path, whatever the EL answers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
